From 3cef9dedc4cc04a7d48d55c80299e7f3d57481b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Twomey <william.twomey@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:55:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: xfs: fix double ILOCK unlock in
 xfs_buffered_write_iomap_begin

The revert of "xfs: use iomap_valid method to detect stale cached
iomaps" (2061a2038206) restored the early xfs_iunlock(ip, XFS_ILOCK_EXCL)
at found_cow. The 6.1.138 merge then brought in stable "xfs: match lock
mode in xfs_buffered_write_iomap_begin()" (upstream bb712842a85d), and
the resolution kept upstream's xfs_iunlock(ip, lockmode) before each
return as well, so the COW path drops the ILOCK twice. The rwsem is
corrupted and the next xfs_ilock() on the inode sleeps forever.

The COW path is reached on shared extents (reflink=1, the mkfs.xfs
default), which overlayfs copy-up creates, so overlayfs on XFS (e.g.
Docker overlay2) hangs in D state on the first chown/chmod of a
copied-up file:

  chown D: xfs_ilock <- xfs_map_blocks <- iomap_do_writepage <- ...
           <- xfs_setattr_size <- xfs_vn_setattr <- ovl_copy_up_metadata

Drop the stale early unlock so the block matches upstream 6.1.y.

Fixes: 4c7f06c5da94 ("Merge 6.1.138 into android14-6.1-lts")
Change-Id: I21fa3ff556269e61e54d0740c2f09a46225622ba
Signed-off-by: Will Twomey <william.twomey@gmail.com>
---
 fs/xfs/xfs_iomap.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/xfs/xfs_iomap.c b/fs/xfs/xfs_iomap.c
index d029284f22e4..99af800f2953 100644
--- a/fs/xfs/xfs_iomap.c
+++ b/fs/xfs/xfs_iomap.c
@@ -1114,7 +1114,6 @@ xfs_buffered_write_iomap_begin(
 	return 0;
 
 found_cow:
-	xfs_iunlock(ip, XFS_ILOCK_EXCL);
 	if (imap.br_startoff <= offset_fsb) {
 		error = xfs_bmbt_to_iomap(ip, srcmap, &imap, flags, 0);
 		if (error)
-- 
2.53.0

